      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "JSON Web Token\nA JSON Web Token (JWT, said \"jot\") is a token\nformat: a set of claims with a signature ([RFC\n7519](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.h\ntml#section-1)). It has three parts, joined by\ndots: the header, the claims, and the\nsignature. Each part is base64url encoded\n([RFC 7519](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc\n7519.html#section-3)). The script in About the\nExamples built this token with a shared\nsecret:\n\n`eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3Mi\nOiJodHRwczovL2lkcC5leGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInN1YiI6In\nN2Yy1sb2FkZXIiLCJhdWQiOiJodHRwczovL2FwaS5leGFt\ncGxlLmNvbSIsImlhdCI6MTc5NDcwMDgwMCwiZXhwIjoxNz\nk0NzA0NDAwfQ.rcEL4KU9STAjyB24nWb1fMzFRPEM-ec53\nvwKRIApr7g`\n\nThe header decodes to `{\"alg\": \"HS256\", \"typ\":\n\"JWT\"}`. The claims decode to `{\"iss\":\n\"https://idp.example.com\", \"sub\":\n\"svc-loader\", \"aud\":\n\"https://api.example.com\", \"iat\": 1794700800,\n\"exp\": 1794704400}`. These five names are\nregistered claims ([RFC 7519](https://www.rfc-\neditor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html#section-4.1)).\nThey are the issuer, the subject, the\naudience, the time of issue, and the time of\nexpiry. The audience is the API that the token\nis for. The times count seconds since\n1970-01-01 UTC. Here 1794700800 is 2026-11-15\n00:00:00 UTC, and the token expires one hour\nlater.\n\nAnyone who holds the token can read the first\ntwo parts. The signature lets the checker\ndetect any change. HS256 is a signature made\nwith a shared secret, by HMAC using SHA-256.\nRS256 is a signature made with a private key,\nby RSA using SHA-256 ([RFC 7518](https://www.r\nfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7518.html#section-3.1)).\nAn API that receives a JWT access token\nverifies the signature, the issuer, the\naudience, and the expiry ([RFC 9068](https://w\nww.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9068.html#section-4))\n.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-5038e1871216",
      "originalText": "JSON Web Token\nA JSON Web Token (JWT, said \"jot\") is a token format: a set of claims with a signature ([RFC 7519](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html#section-1)). It has three parts, joined by dots: the header, the claims, and the signature. Each part is base64url encoded ([RFC 7519](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html#section-3)). The script in About the Examples built this token with a shared secret:\n\n`eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJodHRwczovL2lkcC5leGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsInN1YiI6InN2Yy1sb2FkZXIiLCJhdWQiOiJodHRwczovL2FwaS5leGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsImlhdCI6MTc5NDcwMDgwMCwiZXhwIjoxNzk0NzA0NDAwfQ.rcEL4KU9STAjyB24nWb1fMzFRPEM-ec53vwKRIApr7g`\n\nThe header decodes to `{\"alg\": \"HS256\", \"typ\": \"JWT\"}`. The claims decode to `{\"iss\": \"https://idp.example.com\", \"sub\": \"svc-loader\", \"aud\": \"https://api.example.com\", \"iat\": 1794700800, \"exp\": 1794704400}`. These five names are registered claims ([RFC 7519](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7519.html#section-4.1)). They are the issuer, the subject, the audience, the time of issue, and the time of expiry. The audience is the API that the token is for. The times count seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC. Here 1794700800 is 2026-11-15 00:00:00 UTC, and the token expires one hour later.\n\nAnyone who holds the token can read the first two parts. The signature lets the checker detect any change. HS256 is a signature made with a shared secret, by HMAC using SHA-256. RS256 is a signature made with a private key, by RSA using SHA-256 ([RFC 7518](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7518.html#section-3.1)). An API that receives a JWT access token verifies the signature, the issuer, the audience, and the expiry ([RFC 9068](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9068.html#section-4)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "jwt"
      }
    },
