    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9985564000,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-426ea41c0f15",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 736.0,
      "y": 2460.0,
      "strokeColor": "#0F172A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 377.99999999999994,
      "height": 1012.5,
      "seed": 774566,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Standards\nA standard defines the messages\nbetween the caller and the\nservice. The table compares seven\nof them:\n\n| Standard | Defined by | What the\ncaller presents |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Basic | [RFC 7617](https://www.r\nfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7617.html) |\nThe user ID and the password,\njoined by a colon and base64\nencoded |\n| API key | Each API; the [OpenAPI\n](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3\n.1.0.html#security-scheme-object)\nformat for describing HTTP APIs\ncovers it | A secret string in a\nheader, a query parameter, or a\ncookie |\n| OAuth 2.0 | [RFC 6749](https://w\nww.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html\n) | An access token |\n| OpenID Connect | [OpenID Foundat\nion](https://openid.net/specs/open\nid-connect-core-1_0.html) | An ID\ntoken, which is a JWT |\n| SAML 2.0 | [OASIS](https://docs.\noasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2\n.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.htm\nl) | An XML assertion about the\nuser |\n| Kerberos | [RFC 4120](https://ww\nw.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4120.html)\n| A ticket from the key\ndistribution center |\n| Mutual TLS (Transport Layer\nSecurity) | [RFC 8446](https://www\n.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html)\n| A certificate, in the TLS\nhandshake |\n\nThe nodes below follow the order\nof the table.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 22.5,
      "containerId": "node-426ea41c0f15",
      "originalText": "Standards\nA standard defines the messages between the caller and the service. The table compares seven of them:\n\n| Standard | Defined by | What the caller presents |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Basic | [RFC 7617](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7617.html) | The user ID and the password, joined by a colon and base64 encoded |\n| API key | Each API; the [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html#security-scheme-object) format for describing HTTP APIs covers it | A secret string in a header, a query parameter, or a cookie |\n| OAuth 2.0 | [RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html) | An access token |\n| OpenID Connect | [OpenID Foundation](https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html) | An ID token, which is a JWT |\n| SAML 2.0 | [OASIS](https://docs.oasis-open.org/security/saml/Post2.0/sstc-saml-tech-overview-2.0.html) | An XML assertion about the user |\n| Kerberos | [RFC 4120](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4120.html) | A ticket from the key distribution center |\n| Mutual TLS (Transport Layer Security) | [RFC 8446](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html) | A certificate, in the TLS handshake |\n\nThe nodes below follow the order of the table.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "authentication-standards"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
