    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1476094811,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-505032eaf8a3",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1332.0,
      "y": 1940.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 297.5,
      "seed": 742365,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "API Key\nAn API key is a secret string that the owner\nof an API issues to a caller. The caller sends\nthe same string with every request. Each API\nchooses where the key goes. The [OpenAPI speci\nfication](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0\n.html#security-scheme-object) describes a key\nwith two settings: `name`, which is the\nheader, query parameter, or cookie that\ncarries the key, and `in`, which is `query`,\n`header`, or `cookie`. The specification's own\nexample is `{\"type\": \"apiKey\", \"name\":\n\"api_key\", \"in\": \"header\"}`. It means that the\nrequest carries the header `api_key: <key>`. A\nSnowflake programmatic access token also\ntravels as a secret string with each request.\nStored Secret describes it.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-505032eaf8a3",
      "originalText": "API Key\nAn API key is a secret string that the owner of an API issues to a caller. The caller sends the same string with every request. Each API chooses where the key goes. The [OpenAPI specification](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.0.html#security-scheme-object) describes a key with two settings: `name`, which is the header, query parameter, or cookie that carries the key, and `in`, which is `query`, `header`, or `cookie`. The specification's own example is `{\"type\": \"apiKey\", \"name\": \"api_key\", \"in\": \"header\"}`. It means that the request carries the header `api_key: <key>`. A Snowflake programmatic access token also travels as a secret string with each request. Stored Secret describes it.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "api-key"
      }
    },
    {
