    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4895456171,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-b8e17db7d81b",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1332.0,
      "y": 2200.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 752.5,
      "seed": 944690,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "OAuth 2.0\nThe abstract of [RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-edi\ntor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html) says that OAuth 2.0\nlets an application obtain limited access to\nan HTTP service. The application acts for a\nresource owner, or on its own behalf. The\nframework defines four grant types, which are\nthe ways to get an access token ([RFC 6749](ht\ntps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#sect\nion-1.3)):\n\n- Authorization code: a person approves access\nin a browser.\n- Client credentials: a program uses its own\ncredentials. Programs and Service Accounts\ncovers it.\n- Implicit and resource owner password\ncredentials: [RFC 9700](https://www.rfc-editor\n.org/rfc/rfc9700.html#section-2.4) says that\nclients should not use the implicit grant and\nmust not use the password grant.\n\nThe framework leaves other choices to each\nproduct. The token format is outside its scope\n([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc\n6749.html#section-1.4)). A scope is a list of\nstrings that name the access that a client\nrequests. The authorization server defines the\nstrings ([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org\n/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-3.3)).\n\nSnowflake offers OAuth in two forms. With\nSnowflake OAuth, Snowflake is both the\nauthorization server and the resource server.\nWith External OAuth, a third-party identity\nprovider is the authorization server\n([authentication overview](https://docs.snowfl\nake.com/en/user-guide/security-authentication-\noverview)). Snowflake lists Okta, Microsoft\nEntra ID, and Ping Identity PingFederate as\nexternal authorization servers ([External OAut\nh](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/oa\nuth-ext-overview)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-b8e17db7d81b",
      "originalText": "OAuth 2.0\nThe abstract of [RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html) says that OAuth 2.0 lets an application obtain limited access to an HTTP service. The application acts for a resource owner, or on its own behalf. The framework defines four grant types, which are the ways to get an access token ([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-1.3)):\n\n- Authorization code: a person approves access in a browser.\n- Client credentials: a program uses its own credentials. Programs and Service Accounts covers it.\n- Implicit and resource owner password credentials: [RFC 9700](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9700.html#section-2.4) says that clients should not use the implicit grant and must not use the password grant.\n\nThe framework leaves other choices to each product. The token format is outside its scope ([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-1.4)). A scope is a list of strings that name the access that a client requests. The authorization server defines the strings ([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-3.3)).\n\nSnowflake offers OAuth in two forms. With Snowflake OAuth, Snowflake is both the authorization server and the resource server. With External OAuth, a third-party identity provider is the authorization server ([authentication overview](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/security-authentication-overview)). Snowflake lists Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, and Ping Identity PingFederate as external authorization servers ([External OAuth](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/oauth-ext-overview)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "oauth-2-0"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2562193696,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-ca255db41fa7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1928.8,
