    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1387168346,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-3fbe33e2340d",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 736.0,
      "y": 4020.0,
      "strokeColor": "#0F172A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 377.99999999999994,
      "height": 1732.5,
      "seed": 850929,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Products\nA product is software or a service\nthat runs the standards for you.\nIt keeps the users and the apps,\nsigns people in, and issues the\ntokens. The standards leave some\nchoices open, such as the token\nformat ([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc\n-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#secti\non-1.4)) and the scope strings\n([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor\n.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-3.3)\n). Each product makes its own\nchoices there. The table shows the\nOAuth 2.0 client credentials\nrequest in five products. It also\nshows the request in Snowflake\nOpen Catalog, the hosted Iceberg\nREST catalog that the [Iceberg in\nSnowflake map](../snowflake/iceber\ng/snowflake-iceberg.md) describes.\nEvery request has\n`grant_type=client_credentials`.\n\n| Product | Token endpoint | Names\nthe access with | `expires_in` in\nthe docs' sample |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Auth0 |\n`https://{yourDomain}/oauth/token`\n| `audience`, the identifier of\nthe API | 86400 |\n| Okta, custom authorization\nserver | `https://{yourOktaDomain}\n/oauth2/default/v1/token` |\n`scope`, a custom scope | 3600 |\n| Microsoft Entra ID | `https://lo\ngin.microsoftonline.com/{tenant}/o\nauth2/v2.0/token` | `scope`, the\nURI of the resource plus\n`/.default` | 3599 |\n| Keycloak | `https://<host>/realm\ns/<realm>/protocol/openid-connect/\ntoken` | The roles of the client's\nservice account | 60 |\n| Amazon Cognito | `https://<prefi\nx>.auth.<region>.amazoncognito.com\n/oauth2/token` | `scope`, as\n`<resource server\nidentifier>/<scope name>` | 3600 |\n| Snowflake Open Catalog | `https:\n//<account>.snowflakecomputing.com\n/polaris/api/catalog/v1/oauth/toke\nns` | `scope`, for example\n`PRINCIPAL_ROLE:ALL` | 3600 |\n\nThe values come from the\ndocumentation of [Auth0](https://a\nuth0.com/docs/get-started/authenti\ncation-and-authorization-flow/clie\nnt-credentials-flow/call-your-api-\nusing-the-client-credentials-flow)\n, [Okta](https://developer.okta.co\nm/docs/guides/implement-grant-type\n/clientcreds/main/), [Microsoft\nEntra ID](https://learn.microsoft.\ncom/en-us/entra/identity-platform/\nv2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flow)\n, [Keycloak](https://www.keycloak.\norg/docs/latest/server_admin/),\n[Amazon Cognito](https://docs.aws.\namazon.com/cognito/latest/develope\nrguide/token-endpoint.html), and\n[Snowflake Open Catalog](https://d\nocs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/ta\nbles-iceberg-configure-catalog-int\negration-rest-check-config).",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 22.5,
      "containerId": "node-3fbe33e2340d",
      "originalText": "Products\nA product is software or a service that runs the standards for you. It keeps the users and the apps, signs people in, and issues the tokens. The standards leave some choices open, such as the token format ([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-1.4)) and the scope strings ([RFC 6749](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-3.3)). Each product makes its own choices there. The table shows the OAuth 2.0 client credentials request in five products. It also shows the request in Snowflake Open Catalog, the hosted Iceberg REST catalog that the [Iceberg in Snowflake map](../snowflake/iceberg/snowflake-iceberg.md) describes. Every request has `grant_type=client_credentials`.\n\n| Product | Token endpoint | Names the access with | `expires_in` in the docs' sample |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Auth0 | `https://{yourDomain}/oauth/token` | `audience`, the identifier of the API | 86400 |\n| Okta, custom authorization server | `https://{yourOktaDomain}/oauth2/default/v1/token` | `scope`, a custom scope | 3600 |\n| Microsoft Entra ID | `https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant}/oauth2/v2.0/token` | `scope`, the URI of the resource plus `/.default` | 3599 |\n| Keycloak | `https://<host>/realms/<realm>/protocol/openid-connect/token` | The roles of the client's service account | 60 |\n| Amazon Cognito | `https://<prefix>.auth.<region>.amazoncognito.com/oauth2/token` | `scope`, as `<resource server identifier>/<scope name>` | 3600 |\n| Snowflake Open Catalog | `https://<account>.snowflakecomputing.com/polaris/api/catalog/v1/oauth/tokens` | `scope`, for example `PRINCIPAL_ROLE:ALL` | 3600 |\n\nThe values come from the documentation of [Auth0](https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/authentication-and-authorization-flow/client-credentials-flow/call-your-api-using-the-client-credentials-flow), [Okta](https://developer.okta.com/docs/guides/implement-grant-type/clientcreds/main/), [Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/v2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flow), [Keycloak](https://www.keycloak.org/docs/latest/server_admin/), [Amazon Cognito](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/token-endpoint.html), and [Snowflake Open Catalog](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/tables-iceberg-configure-catalog-integration-rest-check-config).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "identity-products"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
