    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8265498348,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-b07a1c521292",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1332.0,
      "y": 4020.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 507.5,
      "seed": 571221,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Microsoft Entra ID\nMicrosoft Entra ID is a cloud service for\nidentity and access management ([Microsoft Lea\nrn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/fu\nndamentals/what-is-entra#microsoft-entra-id)).\nMicrosoft announced on 11 July 2023 that Azure\nActive Directory is now Microsoft Entra ID\n([name change](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-\nus/entra/fundamentals/new-name)). An app must\nbe registered with a tenant. The registration\ncreates the application object, the global\ntemplate. In each tenant where the app runs, a\nservice principal is its local representation\n([apps and service principals](https://learn.m\nicrosoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/app\n-objects-and-service-principals)).\n\nIn the client credentials flow, an app signs\nin with a shared secret, a certificate, or a\nfederated credential ([client credentials flow\n](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/iden\ntity-platform/v2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flo\nw)). A federated credential comes from another\nidentity provider. A managed identity gives an\nAzure resource an Entra identity with no\ncredentials to manage ([managed identities](ht\ntps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity\n/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview))\n.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-b07a1c521292",
      "originalText": "Microsoft Entra ID\nMicrosoft Entra ID is a cloud service for identity and access management ([Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/fundamentals/what-is-entra#microsoft-entra-id)). Microsoft announced on 11 July 2023 that Azure Active Directory is now Microsoft Entra ID ([name change](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/fundamentals/new-name)). An app must be registered with a tenant. The registration creates the application object, the global template. In each tenant where the app runs, a service principal is its local representation ([apps and service principals](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/app-objects-and-service-principals)).\n\nIn the client credentials flow, an app signs in with a shared secret, a certificate, or a federated credential ([client credentials flow](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/v2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flow)). A federated credential comes from another identity provider. A managed identity gives an Azure resource an Entra identity with no credentials to manage ([managed identities](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "microsoft-entra-id"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8182561382,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-d1081e351fbe",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1320.0,
      "y": 4280.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220,
      "seed": 692692,
