      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Keycloak\nKeycloak is open-source identity and access\nmanagement software\n([keycloak.org](https://www.keycloak.org/)).\nIt supports OpenID Connect, OAuth 2.0, and\nSAML, and its license is Apache 2.0 ([LICENSE]\n(https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak/blob/mai\nn/LICENSE.txt)). A realm manages a set of\nusers, credentials, roles, and groups. Realms\nare isolated from each other ([server\nadministration guide](https://www.keycloak.org\n/docs/latest/server_admin/#core-concepts-and-t\nerms)). A client with Client authentication\nand Service accounts roles enabled can use the\nclient credentials grant. The service account\nof that client must hold the roles that the\nclient needs.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d1081e351fbe",
      "originalText": "Keycloak\nKeycloak is open-source identity and access management software ([keycloak.org](https://www.keycloak.org/)). It supports OpenID Connect, OAuth 2.0, and SAML, and its license is Apache 2.0 ([LICENSE](https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak/blob/main/LICENSE.txt)). A realm manages a set of users, credentials, roles, and groups. Realms are isolated from each other ([server administration guide](https://www.keycloak.org/docs/latest/server_admin/#core-concepts-and-terms)). A client with Client authentication and Service accounts roles enabled can use the client credentials grant. The service account of that client must hold the roles that the client needs.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "keycloak"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
