      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Programs and Service Accounts\nA program cannot type a password\nor approve a prompt on a phone. It\nsigns in with a secret or a\nprivate key that it holds, or with\nan identity that its platform\ngives it. Service Account Names\nsays what each platform calls such\nan identity. Client Credentials\nFlow shows the usual exchange of a\ncredential for a short-lived\ntoken. Stored Secret, Private Key,\nand Platform Identity describe the\nthree ways that a program proves\nwho it is. Choosing a Credential\ncompares them.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 22.5,
      "containerId": "node-552e0ed2baac",
      "originalText": "Programs and Service Accounts\nA program cannot type a password or approve a prompt on a phone. It signs in with a secret or a private key that it holds, or with an identity that its platform gives it. Service Account Names says what each platform calls such an identity. Client Credentials Flow shows the usual exchange of a credential for a short-lived token. Stored Secret, Private Key, and Platform Identity describe the three ways that a program proves who it is. Choosing a Credential compares them.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "programs-and-service-accounts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7880613212,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-d48a5a521b98",
