      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Leaked Secret\nA stored secret works for anyone who finds it.\nSnowflake's comparison table says that anyone\nwho holds a compromised PAT can impersonate\nthe application. GitHub's secret scanner\ndetects leaked Snowflake PATs in public\nrepositories, disables them, and notifies\nSnowflake administrators ([choosing authentica\ntion](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide\n/security-authentication-overview#choosing-aut\nhentication-for-service-to-service-application\ns)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-95f09f192db7",
      "originalText": "Leaked Secret\nA stored secret works for anyone who finds it. Snowflake's comparison table says that anyone who holds a compromised PAT can impersonate the application. GitHub's secret scanner detects leaked Snowflake PATs in public repositories, disables them, and notifies Snowflake administrators ([choosing authentication](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/security-authentication-overview#choosing-authentication-for-service-to-service-applications)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "leaked-secret"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
