      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "About the Examples\nThe values in this map come from three places. The\nfirst place is the examples in the RFCs and in the\nvendor documentation, which are linked where they\nappear. The second place is public pages that\nanyone can fetch. The map used the pages that these\ncommands return, read on 2026-11-15:\n\n```bash\ncurl -i https://api.github.com/user\ncurl https://accounts.google.com/.well-known/openid\n-configuration\ncurl https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/v2.0/\n.well-known/openid-configuration\ncurl https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com/.w\nell-known/openid-configuration\ncurl https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com/.w\nell-known/jwks\n```\n\nThe third place is this script. It ran with Python\n3.12 and the `cryptography` package 50.0.2:\n\n```python\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport json\n\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import hashes,\nserialization\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric\nimport padding, rsa\n\n\ndef b64url(raw):\nreturn\nbase64.urlsafe_b64encode(raw).rstrip(b\"=\").decode()\n\n\ndef b64url_decode(text):\nreturn base64.urlsafe_b64decode(text + \"=\" *\n(-len(text) % 4))\n\n\ndef part(obj):\nreturn b64url(json.dumps(obj, separators=(\",\",\n\":\")).encode())\n\n\nclaims = {\n\"iss\": \"https://idp.example.com\",\n\"sub\": \"svc-loader\",\n\"aud\": \"https://api.example.com\",\n\"iat\": 1794700800,\n\"exp\": 1794704400,\n}\nsigning_input = part({\"alg\": \"HS256\", \"typ\":\n\"JWT\"}) + \".\" + part(claims)\nmac = hmac.new(b\"shared-secret\",\nsigning_input.encode(), hashlib.sha256).digest()\ntoken = signing_input + \".\" + b64url(mac)\nprint(token)\nfor piece in token.split(\".\")[:2]:\nprint(json.loads(b64url_decode(piece)))\nagain = hmac.new(b\"shared-secret\",\nsigning_input.encode(), hashlib.sha256).digest()\nprint(\"valid:\", hmac.compare_digest(again,\nb64url_decode(token.split(\".\")[2])))\n\nkey =\nrsa.generate_private_key(public_exponent=65537,\nkey_size=2048)\npublic_der = key.public_key().public_bytes(\nserialization.Encoding.DER,\nserialization.PublicFormat.SubjectPublicKeyInfo\n)\nfingerprint = \"SHA256:\" + base64.b64encode(hashlib.\nsha256(public_der).digest()).decode()\naccount, user = \"MYORG-MYACCOUNT\", \"SVC_LOADER\"\nclaims = {\n\"iss\": f\"{account}.{user}.{fingerprint}\",\n\"sub\": f\"{account}.{user}\",\n\"iat\": 1794700800,\n\"exp\": 1794704400,\n}\nsigning_input = part({\"alg\": \"RS256\", \"typ\":\n\"JWT\"}) + \".\" + part(claims)\nsignature = key.sign(signing_input.encode(),\npadding.PKCS1v15(), hashes.SHA256())\nkey.public_key().verify(signature,\nsigning_input.encode(), padding.PKCS1v15(),\nhashes.SHA256())\nprint(len(fingerprint), \"characters in\",\nfingerprint)\nprint(json.dumps(claims, indent=1))\nprint(len(signature), \"signature bytes =\",\nlen(b64url(signature)), \"characters\")\n```\n\nThe first part prints the JWT in the JSON Web Token\nnode, and it prints the same token on every run.\nThe second part makes a new 2048-bit key on every\nrun. The fingerprint and the signature change with\neach run, and their lengths stay the same. The time\n1794700800 is 2026-11-15 00:00:00 UTC.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-dd9eba267178",
      "originalText": "About the Examples\nThe values in this map come from three places. The first place is the examples in the RFCs and in the vendor documentation, which are linked where they appear. The second place is public pages that anyone can fetch. The map used the pages that these commands return, read on 2026-11-15:\n\n```bash\ncurl -i https://api.github.com/user\ncurl https://accounts.google.com/.well-known/openid-configuration\ncurl https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/v2.0/.well-known/openid-configuration\ncurl https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com/.well-known/openid-configuration\ncurl https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com/.well-known/jwks\n```\n\nThe third place is this script. It ran with Python 3.12 and the `cryptography` package 50.0.2:\n\n```python\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport json\n\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import hashes, serialization\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric import padding, rsa\n\n\ndef b64url(raw):\n    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(raw).rstrip(b\"=\").decode()\n\n\ndef b64url_decode(text):\n    return base64.urlsafe_b64decode(text + \"=\" * (-len(text) % 4))\n\n\ndef part(obj):\n    return b64url(json.dumps(obj, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode())\n\n\nclaims = {\n    \"iss\": \"https://idp.example.com\",\n    \"sub\": \"svc-loader\",\n    \"aud\": \"https://api.example.com\",\n    \"iat\": 1794700800,\n    \"exp\": 1794704400,\n}\nsigning_input = part({\"alg\": \"HS256\", \"typ\": \"JWT\"}) + \".\" + part(claims)\nmac = hmac.new(b\"shared-secret\", signing_input.encode(), hashlib.sha256).digest()\ntoken = signing_input + \".\" + b64url(mac)\nprint(token)\nfor piece in token.split(\".\")[:2]:\n    print(json.loads(b64url_decode(piece)))\nagain = hmac.new(b\"shared-secret\", signing_input.encode(), hashlib.sha256).digest()\nprint(\"valid:\", hmac.compare_digest(again, b64url_decode(token.split(\".\")[2])))\n\nkey = rsa.generate_private_key(public_exponent=65537, key_size=2048)\npublic_der = key.public_key().public_bytes(\n    serialization.Encoding.DER, serialization.PublicFormat.SubjectPublicKeyInfo\n)\nfingerprint = \"SHA256:\" + base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(public_der).digest()).decode()\naccount, user = \"MYORG-MYACCOUNT\", \"SVC_LOADER\"\nclaims = {\n    \"iss\": f\"{account}.{user}.{fingerprint}\",\n    \"sub\": f\"{account}.{user}\",\n    \"iat\": 1794700800,\n    \"exp\": 1794704400,\n}\nsigning_input = part({\"alg\": \"RS256\", \"typ\": \"JWT\"}) + \".\" + part(claims)\nsignature = key.sign(signing_input.encode(), padding.PKCS1v15(), hashes.SHA256())\nkey.public_key().verify(signature, signing_input.encode(), padding.PKCS1v15(), hashes.SHA256())\nprint(len(fingerprint), \"characters in\", fingerprint)\nprint(json.dumps(claims, indent=1))\nprint(len(signature), \"signature bytes =\", len(b64url(signature)), \"characters\")\n```\n\nThe first part prints the JWT in the JSON Web Token node, and it prints the same token on every run. The second part makes a new 2048-bit key on every run. The fingerprint and the signature change with each run, and their lengths stay the same. The time 1794700800 is 2026-11-15 00:00:00 UTC.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "about-the-examples"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "arrow",
      "version": 1,
